From ddbe9933e75217032ce92e38b0d3432e02f8f869 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: consnop <consnop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:18:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Serve the dev connection on loopback only, startable from
 adb

The dev connection server bound 0.0.0.0:9000 with no authentication, so
with "Use LAN developer connection" on, anyone on the same Wi-Fi could
install apps and talk to the watch. On a public network that meant
turning Wi-Fi off and going over USB to develop at all.

It now binds 127.0.0.1. A computer reaches it through adb (USB or
wireless debugging, both of which authenticate the computer) with
`adb forward tcp:9000 tcp:9000`. Release builds keep upstream's
DUMP-gated DevConnectionReceiver so the computer can also start the
server over adb; the other three QA receivers stay removed.

The watch menu no longer lists the phone's network addresses, which
cannot reach the server anymore. That listing is what closed the app
where the UDP filter is installed (NetworkInterface.getNetworkInterfaces()
returning null), so the KNOWN_ISSUES entry goes. A jvm test fails if the
server becomes reachable on a non-loopback address.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
